annote = {fiat or command regions - boundaries drawn by humans. "a form of sampling of the underlying social reality." Analyses may be artifacts of boundaries used.

area object topology: may be overlapping. May be isolated from each other. May have holes. an object can be a collection of disconnected areas.

planar enforcement: when all the area objects mesh / cover the whole surface and exhaust the study region. 

boundary storage: with planar enforced polygons, each polygon stores its bounding vertices, so all non-study-area-edge vertices are stored twice. Makes errors likely.

