Fragmentation/patches. 

measures of spatial pattern

Autocorrelation. weights matrix. 
Neighbor definitions: queen's, rook's, distance to centroid/skeleton center, nearest neighbor, Delaunay-based, "lag-two" once removed neighbors. Distance-based: inverse distance influence calculation. length of shared boundary. Choice of spatial weights scheme is key step in analysis.

moran's I
2nd numerator: covariance term. Measure of correlation. key point: if most of the pairs (allowed through the weights matrix filter) are on the same side of the mean, Moran's I will be positive, and there will be positive autocorrelation.
Moran scatterplot: plot between polygon values and the aggregated values of their neighbors
Moran's I is effectively the correlation coefficient for the relationship between the attribute values and the local mean attribute values

Moran's I significance and error bars can be determined by a monte carlo procedure
interesting description: scale of influence of autocorrelated region (Moran's I at different spatial lags; Fig 7.10)

Geary's C.
joins count test: county the number of occurrences of neighboring pairs of polygons in the various different possible categories.},
